; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i2.wp.com/sirisgraphics.com/wp-content/uploads/Divine-Lotus-Art-4.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T12:50:18-07:00","id":670040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=669945#post669945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd suggest sticking with Dawn or Twilight, and also including some gold, yellow, red, or orange in the anima.<br /> <br /> I do not think green is appropriate for a Solar, though. That association is just too Infernal.<br /> (Likewise, I don't consider brown or black appropriate).</div> </div> </div> </div>Idk man, if a Zenith wants Mount Meru in their anima to represent the holiness, stability and resilience of the pole of Earth... Or if a Night wants their anima to be a cloud of darkness pierced and burned away by shafts of righteous light... Or if an Eclipse wants their anima to be a silver-antlered and golden taloned dragon with emerald scales and a line of fire running down it's back while it is holding a scroll in one hand and a pearl in the other...<br /> <br /> I'd let them have it and applaud their creativity. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T12:50:20-07:00","id":670041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=670003#post670003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not like, super baleful green fire all the time or anything like that, but if you wanted to have a golden tree topped with glittering green leaves, why not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah I was thinking of just diffuse green sunlight. A green object in your iconic anima is quite different.<br /> <br /> And yeah, TidyGamer you've convinced me about the cloud of darkness. That's a cool image.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-18-2015, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T13:02:36-07:00","id":670052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=669873#post669873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here, what the corebook has to say for us on solar animas color palettes...<br /> <br /> No pink or rose outright mentioned, but between reds, purples, golds and blues, there might be some wiggle room to be found, i think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read the writeup for Master Vikkart of Spith in CB: Dawn. It explicitly notes that his anima is a rosy color.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T13:12:26-07:00","id":670068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=670001#post670001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would y'all really police this? <i>Really?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, to an extent. I'm not going to let anyone have an anima banner that belongs to another exalt type, period. If you aren't a lunar, you aren't going to glow silver at my table no matter how good your explanation is.<br /> <br /> That still leaves an enormous possibility space in which your anima banner is completely reasonable, though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T13:16:23-07:00","id":670073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=670068#post670068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, to an extent. I'm not going to let anyone have an anima banner that belongs to another exalt type, period. If you aren't a lunar, you aren't going to glow silver at my table no matter how good your explanation is.<br /> <br /> That still leaves an enormous possibility space in which your anima banner is completely reasonable, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a feeling Exigents throw a big wrench into the mix, since their animas will probably be all over the place, and the big differentiation will be caste marks.<br /> <br /> That said, I could see &quot;diaphanous white&quot; being <i>mistaken </i>for silver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 09-18-2015, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T13:20:40-07:00","id":670077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Delta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=669925#post669925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If blue isn't too confusing, why would pink be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't say it categorically would be. Said <i>if</i> it]s <i>so</i> pink it's confusing, <i>then</i> is inappropriate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=670001#post670001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion the caste mark is much more important than the anima.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't know it was a contest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=670001#post670001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would y'all really police this? <i>Really?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Would head it off at the pass before anima is presented as excuse to confuse NPCs as to whether character is Solar.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T13:20:52-07:00","id":670078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=670068#post670068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, to an extent. I'm not going to let anyone have an anima banner that belongs to another exalt type, period. If you aren't a lunar, you aren't going to glow silver at my table no matter how good your explanation is.<br /> <br /> That still leaves an enormous possibility space in which your anima banner is completely reasonable, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if your anima is a thunderhead with bright silver lining, as if the sun was behind it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T13:22:29-07:00","id":670079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=670040#post670040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idk man, if a Zenith wants Mount Meru in their anima to represent the holiness, stability and resilience of the pole of Earth... Or if a Night wants their anima to be a cloud of darkness pierced and burned away by shafts of righteous light... Or if an Eclipse wants their anima to be a silver-antlered and golden taloned dragon with emerald scales and a line of fire running down it's back while it is holding a scroll in one hand and a pearl in the other...<br /> <br /> I'd let them have it and applaud their creativity.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In my last Exalted game, the Night Caste in the party had an enormous dragon made of leaves, vines, and flowers as her iconic banner. Its eyes glowed golden, and she was constantly surrounded by flower petals that burst into golden flames as they were shed from the dragon's back like scales. No one ever thought &quot;Hey, she should be a Wood Aspect!&quot; because her non-iconic anima was still muted golds and deep blues, and oh yeah, SHE HAD A NIGHT CASTE MARK ON HER FOREHEAD. XD<br /> <br /> Let your players be creative. It does great things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />&quot;The true object of all human life is play. Earth is a task garden; heaven is a playground.&quot; -G.K. Chesterton","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/53-blackwingedheaven","name":"blackwingedheaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar53_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T13:36:32-07:00","id":670114,"title":"","content":"Honestly I'd assume that in game, if...<br /> \u2022 a solar with a mostly green colored anima...<br /> \u2022 a chosen of secrets...<br /> \u2022 a wood aspect...<br /> \u2022 a slayer caste infernal...<br /> \u2022 a viper totem lunar with a green snake in his anima...<br /> \u2022 and an Abyssal who's anima has green in it...<br /> are all are in one area AND all are flashing iconic AND even if they all have similar visual styles to each other, people would <i>still</i> be able to tell the difference between the exalt types and no one is running the risk of being mistaken for the wrong exalt type.<br /> <br /> If someone thinks they can light up their solar anima that looks like fire and say &quot;Naw dude i'm not an Anethema, I'm a fire aspect!&quot; they're wrong. 99.9% of Creation is gonna run the f away when a maybe-Anethema lights up before they can say a word. The other .1% are the wyld hunt and they're gonna try and murder you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":7195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","user":"TidyGamer","date":". 09-18-2015, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T13:41:10-07:00","id":670119,"title":"","content":"er, rose colored glasses should give you pink headlights in the golden mist?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like my Avatar? Courtesy of<span style=\"color:#0000FF\"> Jen</span>! : <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Anybody want their characters to be experimented on ? </span>post 98<br /> <i>An Exalt is never unarmed.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4018-l-het-esh","name":"L'het'esh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T13:44:26-07:00","id":670125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=670068#post670068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, to an extent. I'm not going to let anyone have an anima banner that belongs to another exalt type, period. If you aren't a lunar, you aren't going to glow silver at my table no matter how good your explanation is.<br /> <br /> That still leaves an enormous possibility space in which your anima banner is completely reasonable, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about Eclipses? They're supposed to shine as symbols of unity. They can have odd glows, so long as they aren't cribbing Charms that they shouldn't have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T13:57:42-07:00","id":670141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackwingedheaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=670079#post670079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one ever thought &quot;Hey, she should be a Wood Aspect!&quot; because her non-iconic anima was still muted golds and deep blues, and oh yeah, SHE HAD A NIGHT CASTE MARK ON HER FOREHEAD. XD</div> </div> </div> </div>I once had a player who gave himself a red anima and was constantly trying to pass himself off as a Fire Aspect. After nearly dying a half dozen times he tried calling bullshit on me. (I'm paraphrasing here, obviously)<br /> <br /> Him: What the hell? I have the jade artifacts and I'm rolling well on my disguise roll. How do the hell do they keep knowing I'm not a Dragon-Blooded?<br /> Me: Because you keep flaring your anima every time you try to pass yourself.<br /> Him: Why does that matter? I told you, it's red and shit, it should look like a Fire Aspect's.<br /> Me: Flaring your anima also causes your caste mark to appear.<br /> Him: ...<br /> Him: ...goddamnit.<br /> <br /> He abandoned that ploy shortly afterwards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T14:02:36-07:00","id":670145,"title":"","content":"Do people remember how the Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time had that recurring visual element of somebody holding out their hands and a ball of light growing in the middle of it? Also the fairies. Oh, better yet, lightsabers, they have a similar thing; that image of a white core with a different colour playing at the edges of it? I've never actually been sure if that kind of effect is physically possible... maybe for some kind of neon lights? Even then, I don't know enough about optics for how it makes sense, and it's probably still not as dramatic as that Legend of Zelda light ball. Anyway, I could see even the Zenith anima as a solid white core with most other colours able to play around the edges with varying degrees of thickness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T14:04:22-07:00","id":670148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=670141#post670141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I once had a player who gave himself a red anima and was constantly trying to pass himself off as a Fire Aspect. After nearly dying a half dozen times he tried calling bullshit on me. (I'm paraphrasing here, obviously)<br /> <br /> Him: What the hell? I have the jade artifacts and I'm rolling well on my disguise roll. How do the hell do they keep knowing I'm not a Dragon-Blooded?<br /> Me: Because you keep flaring your anima every time you try to pass yourself.<br /> Him: Why does that matter? I told you, it's red and shit, it should look like a Fire Aspect's.<br /> Me: Flaring your anima also causes your caste mark to appear.<br /> Him: ...<br /> Him: ...goddamnit.<br /> <br /> He abandoned that ploy shortly afterwards.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep. This is why I mentioned in my original comment with &quot;You can be creative with your Tometic Anima, but everyone who looks at you will still know you are a *insert Exalt Type here*&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm okay with out of the box creativity for things that have no mechanical effect. I am not okay with trying to subvert certain aspects of the game under that guise. If you want to pass as another Exalt Type, there are Sorcery and Martial Arts that will let you do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":".  Added the word Tometic. 09-18-2015, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T14:12:51-07:00","id":670158,"title":"","content":"I'm somewhat strict with the Animas' overall glow staying close to the descriptions of each Caste. I'm OK with more unusual colors in the actual icon of their totemic manifestation, though.<br /> <br /> So, in my games, a Zenith's anima is colored in sunlight-like whites and golds, but the totemic manifestation that appears in it when the anima reaches that point could be a black lotus surrounded by blood mandalas or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T14:17:43-07:00","id":670164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=670077#post670077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't know it was a contest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying it's a contest, I'm saying that as there's no differentiation in Caste marks from Exalt to Exalt, that's the easiest indicator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T14:20:38-07:00","id":670168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=669978#post669978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the general tenor of the thread, not that another bit of support was really needed, but hey:<br /> <br /> The epithet &quot;rosy-fingered Dawn&quot; appears no small number of times in the Odyssey. If it's good enough for Homer, it's probably good enough for your Solar's anima banner. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but then the Odyssey also speaks of &quot;wine-dark seas&quot;, so make of that what you'll will. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T14:35:46-07:00","id":670178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=670078#post670078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What if your anima is a thunderhead with bright silver lining, as if the sun was behind it</div> </div> </div> </div>For real edge cases, which I've only encountered a tiny handful of times, I use the rubric of &quot;if they turned their back and flared their anima, would a reasonably informed savant be confused as to what sort of Exalt type they are?&quot;<br /> <br /> If the answer is &quot;yes&quot; then I will probably disapprove of it. I know a lot of people in the thread are saying &quot;the Caste mark is most important&quot; and they aren't wrong, but the Caste mark is like the size of a silver dollar and not easily visible in many cases, whereas an anima banner is something you can discern from literally tens of miles away if the circumstances are right. It is true that having a Caste mark <i>at all</i> marks you out as &quot;not a Dragon-Blooded, therefore often problematic&quot; but I genuinely do think the anima banner alone should distinguish your Exalt type readily, especially at bonfire level.<br /> <br /> That said, this gives you an enormous possibility space to work with, and I'm even willing to bend it all the way to &quot;sure, this looks sort of Fire Aspect-y when I describe it, but in-universe the glory of the sun is readily apparent to all looking at it; someone who sees me flare this from a long way away will <i>not</i> confuse me with someone who has Hesiesh's aspect.&quot;<br /> <br /> Even that has limits, tho.<br /> <br /> Oh, and as for Coiks story, which is a cool story... I don't think any dev has ever spoken to it one way or the other (could be wrong, the devs have spilled a lot of ink talking about the game) but I've always felt that the entire reason you can't easily hide a Caste mark is precisely to head off clever boots players trying to have their anima banner cake and also eat the cake of &quot;No, really, I'm not a Solar.&quot; I've let people try to fake being another Exalt type without using a Resplendent Destiny, but if they want to flare their banner and still get away with it... I've let that happen <i>once</i>, and it involved someone willing to invest a lot of XP into custom Stealth Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T14:41:49-07:00","id":670179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=670168#post670168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but then the Odyssey also speaks of &quot;wine-dark seas&quot;, so make of that what you'll will. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>There's interesting stuff out there about how cultures develop terms for the color blue basically last of all colors, since it's less prevalent in nature. Red is third, after black and white.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T15:02:03-07:00","id":670212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=670179#post670179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's interesting stuff out there about how cultures develop terms for the color blue basically last of all colors, since it's less prevalent in nature. Red is third, after black and white.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aye, I remember having my mind blown when I heard about it, myself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <a href=\"http://www.radiolab.org/story/211213-sky-isnt-blue/\" target=\"_blank\">This Radiolab episode</a> introduced me to the notion. If anyone has any other resources on the topic, I'd welcome being pointed in their direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T15:06:11-07:00","id":670214,"title":"","content":"Speaking of different Animas: I quite like that one illustration in the Second Edition core, which makes the Anima look as though the Terrestrial is straight up on fire. It's so vibrant and powerful looking, and does not in the least look like how I picture a Solar Anima regardless of colour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T15:15:44-07:00","id":670217,"title":"","content":"When an exalt I play is inside their armour, plenty of times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T15:26:06-07:00","id":670227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=670214#post670214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of different Animas: I quite like that one illustration in the Second Edition core, which makes the Anima look as though the Terrestrial is straight up on fire. It's so vibrant and powerful looking, and does not in the least look like how I picture a Solar Anima regardless of colour.</div> </div> </div> </div>It made me really sad when I found out terrestrial anima banners were just coloured lights and not physical expressions of their element, as much of the artwork seems to imply.<br /> <br /> When an earth aspect which a swirling dust storm anima goes totemic they don't literally kick up a temporary flurry of sand, it's just white light that moves in a way that's evocative of sand. I much prefer the water anima can literally make you soaking wet kind of vibe, even if it dries supernaturally quickly or something to make it less useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T15:35:00-07:00","id":670233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=670227#post670227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It made me really sad when I found out terrestrial anima banners were just coloured lights and not physical expressions of their element, as much of the artwork seems to imply.<br /> <br /> When an earth aspect which a swirling dust storm anima goes totemic they don't literally kick up a temporary flurry of sand, it's just white light that moves in a way that's evocative of sand. I much prefer the water anima can literally make you soaking wet kind of vibe, even if it dries supernaturally quickly or something to make it less useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always operated under the assumption that this is<i> exactly</i> how anima flux works. The actual rules don't deign to go into details about how their anima flux rips up the terrain, just that it is the raw power of their essence doing the damage, but since their essence is naturally aspected towards their element... I mean, that just makes a lot more <i>sense</i> to me than &quot;they cause damage with hard light.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, holy shit. I used the index to look up what page MoeP: Dragon-Blooded the anima flux rules were on! <i>The index was useful</i>.<br /> <br /> I'm scared. Someone hold me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":4742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","user":"Murcushio","date":". 09-18-2015, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T15:37:36-07:00","id":670236,"title":"","content":"Yeah!<br /> And anima flux damage should look different, depending on aspect. Fire animas burn stuff, Earth animas scour them like sandstorms, Air animas freeze-dry or electro-fry them, Water animas erode them super-fast and leave them soaking, and Wood animas leave stuff looking like a jillion roots broke them up or they got splashed with acid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T15:39:13-07:00","id":670239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=670227#post670227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It made me really sad when I found out terrestrial anima banners were just coloured lights and not physical expressions of their element, as much of the artwork seems to imply.<br /> <br /> When an earth aspect which a swirling dust storm anima goes totemic they don't literally kick up a temporary flurry of sand, it's just white light that moves in a way that's evocative of sand. I much prefer the water anima can literally make you soaking wet kind of vibe, even if it dries supernaturally quickly or something to make it less useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>... What, really? Shit, man, with anima flux and stuff like that, I always thought that Terrestrial Animas were actual elemental expression.<br /> <br /> That's something I might just headcanon, like how in my Creation, Calibration is literally five solid days and nights of darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T16:02:48-07:00","id":670254,"title":"","content":"It would be pretty neat for them to leave physical elemental material behind -- not just the things that were damaged or destroyed by the flux; but pieces of bark or grass or leaves or flower petals; sand or gravel; snow or hail or an invisible (harmless) static charge; soot and ash; a puddle or at least dampness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T20:59:00-07:00","id":670448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=670068#post670068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, to an extent. I'm not going to let anyone have an anima banner that belongs to another exalt type, period.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't there charms that allow an Exalt to do just that?<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm pretty sure there's an Abyssal Intergrity Charm right in the corebooks that does just that. Or a Larceny charm, I'm a bit fuzzy on the details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T21:23:54-07:00","id":670456,"title":"","content":"It's Larceny. But it's not something you get for free, and Abyssals looking like Solars isn't like, say, Lunars looking like DBs.<br /> <br /> I don't think the colour is a big issue though, since you still have the caste mark. So people aren't going to get too confused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T21:30:16-07:00","id":670459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=670456#post670456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's Larceny. But it's not something you get for free, and Abyssals looking like Solars isn't like, say, Lunars looking like DBs.</div> </div> </div> </div>The importance, is the precedent it sets. Which matters quite a bit when one starts creating charms to disguise ones self as a different type of Exalt.<br /> <br /> Which is a perfectly sensible tact to take when you're not sure the irate buddhist witch hunters are going to believe you when you say you're a &quot;godblooded.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T22:00:48-07:00","id":670481,"title":"","content":"Well, I suspect when they wrote that charm, it was supposed to be about the link between Solar and Abyssals (Solars have a mirror charm to look like Abyssals), like the way they have charms that let them use Solar charms (and Solars have a charm that lets them use Abyssal charms). I don't think it's supposed to set a precedent for Dragonblood disguising themselves as Solars.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I'm never sure what the view on disguising your anima is supposed to be. There are a few effects, that are all obscure and specific (or vague). Is it supposed to be something really hard, because it defeats the themes and limitations of using anima banners (ie either you reveal you're an Anathema, or you set fire to stuff around you, so you should only use peripheral essence when it's time to reveal your true power: it is, after all, an expression of your very soul). Or is it supposed to be easy, because, well, if a Lunar can disguise themselves as a cat, why not a Dragonblood?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T22:58:48-07:00","id":670491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=670459#post670459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The importance, is the precedent it sets. Which matters quite a bit when one starts creating charms to disguise ones self as a different type of Exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Abyssals were portrayed in 2nd as basically an evil universe version of the Solar. Essentially the charm was to allow mirror universe Kirk to pretend to be regular Kirk or regular Kirk to pretend to be his mirror universe duplicate. You could make an argument that uses it as a precedent for an Infernal version of the charm, but it is not really setting a precedent for pretending to be other exalt types. There just isn't the same kind of connection between Solar and Dragonblood exaltations as there is between Solars and the Abyssals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T23:12:00-07:00","id":670507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=670239#post670239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... What, really? Shit, man, with anima flux and stuff like that, I always thought that Terrestrial Animas were actual elemental expression.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought they were too: hence why Fire Aspects have to live in stone houses so as to not burn them down. It's certainly a lot more evocative (and, to me, sensible) to say &quot;the Air Aspect's lightning anima shocks you&quot; than &quot;the blue glow damages you... somehow? With, like, dangerous blueness?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T23:19:05-07:00","id":670510,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, I have a dark purple anima on my Lunar, almost black, with silver flashes at the edges. But when there's a silver ring on my forehead and frequently a giant silver owl above me, it's pretty damn obvious.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I've never seen a player try to make their anima look like a different Exalts. They did use to use Disguise of the New Face a lot though (I have that spell).<br /> <br /> Although, there is a PC in my game who is an Eclipse sorceress who made a deal with a forbidden god of fire, and so she has white-hot veins, can summon wings of fire, has a heart of fire that pumps magma around her body (hence the veins) and can shoot fire from her hands. One of the PCs told the bad guys she was called Sesus Ahenduanna, so now all the bad guys think she's a Fire Aspect. Obviously she hasn't flared in front of them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T23:45:38-07:00","id":670515,"title":"","content":"I agree it's not as cool, and in fact in the fanthology story I wrote the DBs anima was literally a windstorm. Sadly it looks like my attempt to make an anthology story with less canon holes has failed.<br /> <br /> The real question is, will this fact that DB animas are just coloured light hold for ex3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T00:15:02-07:00","id":670527,"title":"","content":"The example animas for DB in scroll of Exalts are pretty nice, they don't sound like colored light.<br /> <br /> A crackling blast of lightning briefly outlining incomplete mandala patterns.<br /> A pearly mist spreads from Ghandarva as he spends Essence, in which strange shapes flutter and dance in the madness of their perfection.<br /> A bitterly cold wind accompanied by a patina of ice that spreads across the ground at his feet<br /> <br /> A swirl of brilliant white crystals erupts from the ground at Mnemon\u2019s feet to orbit about her.<br /> As his anima flares, ripples of seismic force emerge from every chakra of Myrrun\u2019s body in pulverizing waves of power. From time to time, the ripples converge into a mirage of scattered lotus petals falling from the path of his movements.<br /> Choking black dust falls from her as she spends Essence, trailing behind her in a phantasmagoria of unnatural erosion. At her anima\u2019s height, she is more trail than woman, a presence defined by her path and the grasping claws ahead of it.<br /> <br /> A coruscating heat-haze that radiates from his body, blurring the air around him.<br /> An enormous flame-etched blade, suspended point down, with a dragon curling around it.<br /> A flame-etched dragon spiraling in upon itself<br /> <br /> An upswelling of waves dozens of feet into the air, finally breaking apart to reveal a dragon with wings like sails<br /> A swirling miasma of dark water, accompanied by the sound of pounding surf.<br /> A darkening of the anima to jet-black, struck through with bright blue lines of cavitation.<br /> <br /> A tree with infinitely, recursively branching limbs that fades away into a haze of leaves on the verge of unveiling some grand and transcendental pattern.<br /> Green vines covered in long thorns whip wildly, lashing those who don\u2019t keep their distance<br /> A swirling mass of razor-sharp black thorns<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=670507#post670507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought they were too: hence why Fire Aspects have to live in stone houses so as to not burn them down. It's certainly a lot more evocative (and, to me, sensible) to say &quot;the Air Aspect's lightning anima shocks you&quot; than &quot;the blue glow damages you... somehow? With, like, dangerous blueness?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically though all DBs like to live in stone houses because it's the only normal material used for building houses that's got the necessary soak to endure an anima flux.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":7195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","user":"TidyGamer","date":". 09-19-2015, 03:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T00:50:34-07:00","id":670553,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that does sound like the anima flux is supposed to be elemental to some extent, rather than generic magic damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T01:56:42-07:00","id":670616,"title":"","content":"Generally, I consider the differences between various Exalt animas to be obvious no matter how much you try to confuse someone.<br /> <br /> A Solar with a red anima cannot possibly be mistaken for a Fire Aspect, as the Solar's anima is TOO RED, its looks fiery but not like actual fire or anything, and something about it just seems more symbolic.<br /> <br /> the Fire Aspects anima......is actual freaking fire, with heat and the usual mix of orange, red and white and so on.<br /> <br /> The Chosen of Mars anima when it flares is not fire, and just a red glow or red strands of fate weaving itself around them.<br /> <br /> now for the difference between a Green Solar, a Wood Aspect, a Chosen of Secrets and an Infernal:<br /> Green Solar: it looks like a deeper softer green than an Infernal, a flame of hope<br /> Wood Aspect: their anima explicitly actual life and things growing around them.<br /> Chosen of Secret: soft green glow and green threads of the Loom as with the other example<br /> Infernal: their green fire burns like hate, it looks sickly and yellowish and there is a whole bunch of cracks or lightning running through it.<br /> <br /> .......perhaps it would be better to find a way to show the animas and how they look than to try to describe them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T02:46:33-07:00","id":670643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=670616#post670616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Solar with a red anima cannot possibly be mistaken for a Fire Aspect, as the Solar's anima is TOO RED, its looks fiery but not like actual fire or anything, and something about it just seems more symbolic.<br /> <br /> the Fire Aspects anima......is actual freaking fire, with heat and the usual mix of orange, red and white and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>For visual examples...<br /> <br /> A Solar whose anima happens to be red.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://vignette2.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/a/a1/Kaioken!.jpg/revision/20110403074517\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> A Fire Aspect<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://blog.honeyfeed.fm/wp-content/uploads/2015/01/Portgas-D.-Ace-500x419.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> At least that was my initial thought. The Kaioken vs Actually On Fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T03:46:07-07:00","id":670738,"title":"","content":"My concern about anima color is &quot;does that guy miles away can know that it's an Anathema or not&quot;. I don't mind colors in the banner but the basic color must link to the patron deity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3053-ikumo","name":"Ikumo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T04:33:09-07:00","id":670781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ikumo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=670738#post670738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My concern about anima color is &quot;does that guy miles away can know that it's an Anathema or not&quot;. I don't mind colors in the banner but the basic color must link to the patron deity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always assumed you couldn't see Dragonblooded Anima from miles away. Thus if you see the glow of Anima in the Sky, it's probably a Solar or a Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T05:34:50-07:00","id":670816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=670781#post670781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always assumed you couldn't see Dragonblooded Anima from miles away.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're two, three miles distant from a bonfire taller than a man on a flat plain, you're gonna see it, even if you can't make out the guy standing in the middle of it. And unless he's competing with a Solar for the light show, he'll probably be the brightest thing around when it's dark out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T06:40:38-07:00","id":670916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=670507#post670507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought they were too: hence why Fire Aspects have to live in stone houses so as to not burn them down.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always been leery about that specific anima; I don't think Fire Aspect anima banners flaring should be able to start actual fires of any consequence, although of course they're still going to tear up the landscape and inflict awful burns on the people wading into them.<br /> <br /> It's a verisimilitude thing. Among other things, I don't ever want there to be a situation where a Fire Aspect is afraid to flare because it means they're going to burn down the entire town, or because their Legion is fighting in the middle of summer, in a giant plain of very dry, very flammable grass on a windy day, and their General <i>orders</i> them not to flare because she'd rather not deal with a giant raging wildfire that can easily spin out of control. Conversely, I don't want them to be able to easily use it as an offensive weapon beyond the normal rules provided by anima flux.<br /> <br /> It's a problem the other four Aspect types don't have I don't think it should be dropped on the Fire Aspects. (This goes out the window with Elemental Bolt Attack, of course, but that's a Charm, not your anima.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":4742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","user":"Murcushio","date":". 09-19-2015, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T06:53:53-07:00","id":670922,"title":"","content":"&quot;Other <i>three</i> Aspects?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T08:10:56-07:00","id":670958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=670922#post670922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Other <i>three</i> Aspects?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Motherfucking <i>Sidereals</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T09:11:55-07:00","id":671010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=670916#post670916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've always been leery about that specific anima; I don't think Fire Aspect anima banners flaring should be able to start actual fires of any consequence, although of course they're still going to tear up the landscape and inflict awful burns on the people wading into them.<br /> <br /> It's a verisimilitude thing. Among other things, I don't ever want there to be a situation where a Fire Aspect is afraid to flare because it means they're going to burn down the entire town, or because their Legion is fighting in the middle of summer, in a giant plain of very dry, very flammable grass on a windy day, and their General <i>orders</i> them not to flare because she'd rather not deal with a giant raging wildfire that can easily spin out of control. Conversely, I don't want them to be able to easily use it as an offensive weapon beyond the normal rules provided by anima flux.<br /> <br /> It's a problem the other four Aspect types don't have I don't think it should be dropped on the Fire Aspects. (This goes out the window with Elemental Bolt Attack, of course, but that's a Charm, not your anima.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean nowhere in the rules does it say fire aspects start fires except in two places - fluff and fire aspected charms<br /> <br /> &quot;Rawr I'm a furious Burning Sword! When the Crimson Dragons flair their power, the fire brigades of Creation cower in fear while forests <b>BURN</b>!&quot; Is <i>really</i> just stunt fodder. The anima deals fire damage, but it only sets fires when the player stunts to do so or when it's dramatically appropriate*. Otherwise it's cosmetic. Similarly when an air aspect has an anima that is a freezing aura of cold, they don't need to worry about freezing themselves in a block of ice when fighting underwater. Earth aspects who's animas rip out chunks of stone to orbit them don't have to worry about structural damage in the cave system they're fighting in beyond what damage their anima flux.<br /> <br /> Edit - * dramatically appropriate <i>for NPCs, </i>not PCs that don't want to be the source of massive property damage. This also allows someone playing a fire aspect to have an anima that's less RAWR FIRE BURRRRRN and more &quot;sizzling heat haze&quot; for maybe a socialite type or &quot;the ground cracks and cloud of fragrant incense are released&quot; from a monkish type of character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":7195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","user":"TidyGamer","date":". 09-19-2015, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T10:16:03-07:00","id":671048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=671010#post671010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean nowhere in the rules does it say fire aspects start fires except in two places - fluff and fire aspected charms<br /> <br /> &quot;Rawr I'm a furious Burning Sword! When the Crimson Dragons flair their power, the fire brigades of Creation cower in fear while forests <b>BURN</b>!&quot; Is <i>really</i> just stunt fodder. The anima deals fire damage, but it only sets fires when the player stunts to do so or when it's dramatically appropriate*. Otherwise it's cosmetic. Similarly when an air aspect has an anima that is a freezing aura of cold, they don't need to worry about freezing themselves in a block of ice when fighting underwater. Earth aspects who's animas rip out chunks of stone to orbit them don't have to worry about structural damage in the cave system they're fighting in beyond what damage their anima flux.<br /> <br /> Edit - * dramatically appropriate <i>for NPCs, </i>not PCs that don't want to be the source of massive property damage. This also allows someone playing a fire aspect to have an anima that's less RAWR FIRE BURRRRRN and more &quot;sizzling heat haze&quot; for maybe a socialite type or &quot;the ground cracks and cloud of fragrant incense are released&quot; from a monkish type of character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually TidyGamer its written in the DB manual*. Spend five mote and the duration of the scene you have a corona of flames that don't burn you, but anything else you touch is effected as if by normal fire.Bare handed and grappling attacks made by or against the DB suffer lethal damage equal to essence level, and if its flammable the DB can ignite it by touching it. On the bright side it does look like its more controllable than a few of us have been remembering as it isn't like the town a fire aspect is in will catch fire just from the banner.<br /> <br /> *Manual of Exalted Power: Dragon-Blooded pg117","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T10:47:59-07:00","id":671087,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Fire Aspect anima is the only one that leaves an actual elemental effect in its wake (stuff burning). You would think, for example, that if a Water Aspect unleashed their anima, at the end of the scene anything affected by it would be soaked, covered in water, etc, but that isn't the case. <br /> <br /> My group finds that a bit boring, so we allow for actual elemental effects when someone uses their anima. So a Water Aspect's anima might leave things soaked afterwards, or an Air Aspects might leave things crackling with static electricity or ice cold, an Earth aspect might leave dust or sand covering everything, etc. It's a fairly minor change but it's fairly cool from a visual standpoint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T11:08:16-07:00","id":671144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=671048#post671048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually TidyGamer its written in the DB manual*. Spend five mote and the duration of the scene you have a corona of flames that don't burn you, but anything else you touch is effected as if by normal fire.Bare handed and grappling attacks made by or against the DB suffer lethal damage equal to essence level, and if its flammable the DB can ignite it by touching it. On the bright side it does look like its more controllable than a few of us have been remembering as it isn't like the town a fire aspect is in will catch fire just from the banner.<br /> <br /> *Manual of Exalted Power: Dragon-Blooded pg117</div> </div> </div> </div>That's their anima power, like air aspects' knockoff stormwind rider, earth aspects' improved soak, water aspects' aquatic mobility and wood aspects' treefrog skin. It's something that you have to choose to activate, it's not automatic like anima flux is","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T11:14:47-07:00","id":671152,"title":"","content":"...yeah, when I run games, Terrestrial anima banners are real elemental effects. When you get enough water essence someplace, then you get water, because that's what water is.<br /> <br /> Fire aspects in my games need to worry about burning down the village. This is, I think, intended by the game: Hesieh is the Immaculate Dragon who teaches restraint and patience and the &quot;don't burn down your house to remove a leech&quot; sort of wisdom, and it's noted as a particularly important sort of lesson for Fire Aspects to have. The ability to start a fire that spreads is an ability shared by peasants with torches, I don't feel like giving it to Exalted warrior-princes is unbalancing in any real way.<br /> <br /> Water aspects in my game can conjure water (or, in one memorable case, shards of swirling ice-blades) from nothing to nourish a desert caravan on a long journey, and that water is real water, and nobody drinks it and then hasn't been hydrated because the essence dissipates. It's a handy trick, if the other people in your caravan are desperate enough to brave your tempestuous anima and risk life and limb for a drink.<br /> <br /> Earth aspects in my game can create rocks. If someone wants an anima like Mnemon's and talks to me about it and spends the points on Resources to make it make sense, I'll let them say their anima causes crystals or sharp-edged gemstones in a poetic color that matches the aesthetic they're going for erupt from the ground and orbit them in pretty glittering blades, and I'll let them keep their diamonds afterwards. The Terrestrial Exalted are divinely empowered nobility, I'm okay with them conjuring precious stones or metals for free (though no Magical Materials or gold or silver allowed-there's a reason the Guild uses the silver standard and the Realm uses the Jade one, and I try to play realistically with supply and demand and market forces in my games).<br /> <br /> Wood aspects can similarly create rare and deadly toxins, or plants with useful herbal properties. They can't change their anima in play without serious spiritual growth and change and a character arc to go with it, but if your anima is grape vines erupting from the ground and lashing the people around you with spiny whips...well, I'm not averse to letting you eat some grapes or make some wine. Same goes for deadly nightshade or medicinal herbs: I'm gonna want you to specify what herb it is and what it's medicinal effects are. It'll be handy in certain situations, but not always.<br /> <br /> Air aspects can do the ice-in-the-desert trick with frozen winds, or they can do lightning effects. While they get less &quot;it hangs around after I'm gone&quot; tricks than the other four, their animas in my game are nonetheless real. An Air Aspect who goes into an undersea cavern can go totemic and fill it with breathable air, for instance, in order to create an undersea supervillain lair.<br /> <br /> I like these sort of powers because they encourage players to play cleverly, and they make the animas of the Terrestrial exalted feel like a very grounded, earthy part of the world. The anima displays of the Anathema are just big shiny lights, but the anima banners of the Exalted are the very flesh and blood of Creation reaching out to serve the Dragons' Chosen. The Dragonblooded should feel like part of the world whose power they are channeling, and making their animas real makes them feel more real...and opens up so many more stories! Perhaps some pirates are holding a teenaged Earth aspect prisoner and forcing her to produce rubies for them! Perhaps the Air Aspected craftsman has created a giant cannon fueled by the lightnings of his own anima so that nobody else can operate it! Perhaps there's an outcaste Water aspect who has founded an oasis-citadel in the South and has set herself up as a goddess worshipped by the locals! Perhaps the monk who is hunting you with the Wyld Hunt is afraid to actually fight you with his full strength because his anima has burned the innocent before, and rants furiously at you for using these innocent villagers as human shields!<br /> <br /> There's good stories here!<br /> <br /> If it's just a light show? Not so much.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T11:14:57-07:00","id":671153,"title":"","content":"Hey, maybe if 3E gives 3 anima abilities to every Exalt, Terrestrials will all get &quot;Create [Element]&quot; as an anima power.<br /> Regardless, the elemental effects go in my headcanon.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the effects are different for Dragons of a Different Color. I want Blood Aspects to leave bloodstains on things. Not little smears on their foreheads, but &quot;somebody exsanguinated a dog here&quot; stains. And maybe Blood Aspect anima flux hurts people by sucking blood out of them into the anima!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-19-2015, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T11:34:10-07:00","id":671160,"title":"","content":"I'm all for flavorful anima effects but it gets a little much to me if the water aspect's provides a measurable volume of potable water, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T11:58:04-07:00","id":671174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=671160#post671160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm all for flavorful anima effects but it gets a little much to me if the water aspect's provides a measurable volume of potable water, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? At the most, it would mechanically give a minor bonus to survival rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T12:08:04-07:00","id":671176,"title":"","content":"And Medicine.<br /> <br /> I'd say it isn't at will, it requires spending motes. I'm not sure that generating your own Resources income solely from your wood or earth anima is the best idea, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T12:56:29-07:00","id":671213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=671176#post671176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Medicine.<br /> <br /> I'd say it isn't at will, it requires spending motes. I'm not sure that generating your own Resources income solely from your wood or earth anima is the best idea, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well...yes. It's not at will. Making your anima flare requires spending motes. That's how animas work.<br /> <br /> And seriously, using your anima to make potable water's the least problematic thing on that list. Earth Aspect's the most broken (the one I'd make you actually pay resources for if your anima generates salable goods, though I'd do the same for Wood if your anima was a rare plant or poison you planned on producing in any real quantity). But minor bonuses to Survival rolls? Really? If you're in a blizzard in the North, huddling around the Fire Aspect's warmth and waiting through it is a fun scene! Using your anima to generate water in a desert, or air when you're stuck in a prison cell in a sinking slave galleon, or some spinach to munch during a famine, or a rich swirl of loamy earth in a rocky wasteland you can use to plant crops? That's awesome!<br /> <br /> Now, to be clear, not every terrestrial can do all of these tricks! You pick your anima at chargen! If you're an Earth Aspect and you decide your anima banner is a swirl of stinging razor-edged black volcanic glass, that's really neat! I'll let you gather up piles of black volcanic glass and melt 'em down in a forge to make cool obsidian glass weapons, it might be a useful component in making an artifact or something...but you're not going to be able to sell 'em to the Guild in any huge quantity. If your anima is jagged marble spires erupting from the earth to impale your opponents, I'm fine with the spires sticking around afterwards (seems like you could do some neat landscaping with that anima, maybe make a kickass garden), and maybe you could carve them into statues or sell the blocks of marble, but you're not feeding people in a desert. If your anima is a tear-shaped blades made out of rubies slashing through the air around you, you can sell the rubies (and I'm going to make you buy dots in Resources at chargen), but I'm not gonna let you stunt your anima making marble spires to stand on to get across the Lake of Boiling Lava: your anima is rubies, not stone spires.<br /> <br /> I'm not only fine with the idea of dragonbloods each having one really neat trick, I love the idea: it encourages them to get creative and to try and find situations where they can use that neat trick to their advantage. The Fire Aspect whose anima is a cloud of roiling black smoke illuminated by burning embers is probably going to fight differently than the Fire Aspect whose anima is a shimmering haze of ridiculous heat that ignites anything it comes into contact with! The first guy's probably going to do great at being a sneaky ninja or a beekeeper! The second guy is gonna be good at wrestling or flying through the frozen northern skies in a self-propelled hot air balloon with a metal basket! Both of 'em have to worry about lighting places they're fighting in on fire, but they're going to be inclined to approach their lives in different ways! And I think that's awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T13:32:10-07:00","id":671248,"title":"","content":"That's a good system, and provides so many cool possibilities.<br /> <br /> I think it's fair to let somebody conjure trivial value for no additional Resources Background. Like 11 motes for 1 Resources dot worth of amethyst or malachite or marble. Sure, you can make a Resources 2 income doing that, if you sit around doing it all day instead of an actual job. That's a waste of an Exalt's time and essence, though, so it isn't worth a Background. It does let you bribe somebody, or poison your arrows before a battle, or make the food taste better around your campfire in the far North. (Or make somebody else's food taste awful by mixing sand or ashes or an inappropriate herb into it.)<br /> <br /> &quot;Gaa--&quot; *<i>sploort</i>* &quot;Ugh, what got into my wine!?&quot; *<i>bleck, ptooi</i>*<br /> &quot;The Dragons do not approve of your weakness for the bottle, Kayim.&quot;<br /> &quot;What did lace it with?&quot; *<i>glare</i>*<br /> &quot;Garlic!&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-19-2015, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T15:24:28-07:00","id":671358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the effects are different for Dragons of a Different Color. I want Blood Aspects</div> </div> </div> </div> Terrestrials with an affinity for necromancy have the same Aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T15:28:14-07:00","id":671359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=671358#post671358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Terrestrials with an affinity for necromancy have the same Aspects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Liminals will have Blood Aspects, won't they?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T16:09:42-07:00","id":671412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=671359#post671359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Liminals will have Blood Aspects, won't they?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Dragons of a Different Color may have name changes.<br /> <br /> Or just not exist, who knows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T16:39:21-07:00","id":671484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=671412#post671412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the Dragons of a Different Color may have name changes.<br /> <br /> Or just not exist, who knows.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least to some degree, their fate may be intertwined with that of necromancy. If the EX3 Team decides there's no harm in regular Dragon-Blooded using it, there's less of a point to the Dragons of a Different Color.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T16:12:08-07:00","id":672462,"title":"","content":"As long as the anima is described as &quot;Pink like a mountain sunrise,&quot; or some such, to indicate viewers know it's a Solar anima, I see no reason to disallow this.<br /> <br /> I'm of the opinion that anything that doesn't screw with mechanics or hurt the setting should be largely left to player customization. So, if a player sets out to &quot;disguise&quot; their Solar by making their anima appear to be a Sid or a DB, then I wouldn't allow that. Beyond that, though go nuts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T16:27:04-07:00","id":672467,"title":"","content":"Terrestrial Exalted with an affinity for necromancy might be a thing, but they probably won't be referred to by a cutesy sidebar title all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T16:42:46-07:00","id":672479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=672467#post672467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Terrestrial Exalted with an affinity for necromancy might be a thing, but they probably won't be referred to by a cutesy sidebar title all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also it might get weird since the water version's anima was blood, the wood bone, ect, and we have blood and bone aspects in Liminals.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T19:28:13-07:00","id":672779,"title":"","content":"Marrow Aspect, actually. But yeah they have a Blood Aspect. Last we heard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T04:27:17-07:00","id":673055,"title":"","content":"Dragons of A Different Colour were a shout out to the popular fanon idea of Abyssal Dragon-Blooded.<br /> \u201cTake Necromancy and try to pretend you\u2019re a different Exalt type, that\u2019s basically what Abyssals do!\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 09-22-2015, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T21:54:50-07:00","id":673855,"title":"","content":"I still sort of like the idea of Dragonblooded based on the Elements of the Underworld. If for no other reason than it gives them a connection to the realm of the dead that they are sorely lacking in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T22:10:12-07:00","id":673860,"title":"","content":"It's a kinda sorta interesting concept, my only real stumbling point with dragons of a different color being a thing is that the Dragon Blooded <i>predate</i> the creation of the underworld. Look at the kinds of hoops people have to jump through to corrupt the solar shards into abyssal shards. It just happening &quot;naturally&quot; to dragon bloods sometimes feels like something that's coming from the &quot;dragon blooded aren't REAL exalts like solars, lunars and sidereals&quot; PoV that seemed a fairly common one around the end of 2E's run.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T23:53:25-07:00","id":673898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=673860#post673860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a kinda sorta interesting concept, my only real stumbling point with dragons of a different color being a thing is that the Dragon Blooded <i>predate</i> the creation of the underworld. Look at the kinds of hoops people have to jump through to corrupt the solar shards into abyssal shards. It just happening &quot;naturally&quot; to dragon bloods sometimes feels like something that's coming from the &quot;dragon blooded aren't REAL exalts like solars, lunars and sidereals&quot; PoV that seemed a fairly common one around the end of 2E's run.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh, it's not that bad.<br /> <br /> Dragons of a Different Colour are said to come from mingling ghost-blood and terrestrial-exalt heritages. So of course their death-tainted exaltation post dates the creation of the underworld.<br /> <br /> That taint merely causes sickly pale skin, a wan appearing anima, and the <i>potential </i>to initiate into necromancy in place of sorcery. Only if they do so initate do their anima and aspect markings then start to truly show an underworld stigma; and that's still only descriptive. Besides that, they are no different from other dragon-blooded, as they don't have different charm sets, limit breaks, anima powers, nor anything else such as marks abyssal exalts as distinct from solar exalts.<br /> <br /> They are dragon-blood goths who might learn creepy magic, not undeath-powered exalts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T00:11:31-07:00","id":673901,"title":"","content":"Dragons of a Different Color exist so when a player says &quot;Can my Dynast know Necromancy?&quot; the ST can say &quot;yes&quot; and have a ready interesting sub-plot for the game.<br /> <br /> Since the world of Creation exists to enable stories, not to serve some abstract cosmic principle, this desirable outcome outweighs other potential concerns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T01:56:12-07:00","id":673973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=673860#post673860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a kinda sorta interesting concept, my only real stumbling point with dragons of a different color being a thing is that the Dragon Blooded <i>predate</i> the creation of the underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of the Exalted predate the existence of sorcery as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=673855#post673855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If for no other reason than it gives them a connection to the realm of the dead that they are sorely lacking in.</div> </div> </div> </div>This begs the question of why a connection to the Underworld is relevant or necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T03:21:50-07:00","id":674014,"title":"","content":"I've got no big problem with Dragons of a Different Colour: people like to play their super-special snowflakes, and its doing it in a way that doesn't cause mechanical issues, so I don't mind. It's just not necessary.\u200b<br /> <br /> I recently used one as an antagonist for one story. The fact she was a Dragonblood (and thus one of the rulers of a country that followed a heretical version of the Immaculate Philosophy) came up of course, as did the fact she was a necromantic crime boss who used ghosts to control the underworld (which rather confused the PCs, as they kept mixing it up with the Underworld).<br /> The local people believed she'd been Exalted by the sixth Dragon, the Dragon of the Void, aka the Ebon Dragon (again, confusing the PCs a little), but she didn't actually need to have a weird anima banner for that to work (she perpetuated the idea to keep people scared, so could have done that anyway with a regular Wood Aspect anima banner).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T01:56:50-07:00","id":676200,"title":"","content":"Shadowlands Circle Necromancy is ludicrously powerful outside of Celestial Exalted hands with some serious &quot;perfect or die&quot; effects as long as you've got someone to make Defend Other actions for you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T02:03:54-07:00","id":676205,"title":"","content":"Ah yes, the spell that does damage equal to your health levels, or something like that. Void Mirror Inversion? I forget off the top of my head. It's also an extremely boring spell, compared to shooting obsidian butterflies at people or making spines shoot out of the ground to impale them with.<br /> <br /> That's just bad mechanics though, rather than an issue with the idea of DBs having necromancy. One would hope/assume that in 3rd ed, they won't write such overpowered spells.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T02:28:08-07:00","id":676218,"title":"","content":"That's just the worst example, none of the direct attack spells (I'm not counting Hungry Creeping Shadow for this) have any interaction with DV.<br /> <br /> Edit: The part where I blame this on Shadowlands Circle Necromancy specifically is that it negates the possibility of Countermagic that's not from another Necromancer or a Celestial Circle Sorcerer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 09-24-2015, 05:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T02:46:17-07:00","id":676238,"title":"","content":"Ah, I see. That's a fair point, as it means other DBs can't counter it.<br /> I don't know if that will still be the case in 3rd ed though. \u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T05:31:32-07:00","id":676323,"title":"","content":"I suspect that 3e Necromancy will be an Underworld Initiation to sorcery given that we already know of the existence of a Wyld Initiation. If that's the case it seems unlikely that being from a death tainted bloodline will be the only way for them to get it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T05:58:11-07:00","id":676335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=672479#post672479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also it might get weird since the water version's anima was blood, the wood bone, ect, and we have blood and bone aspects in Liminals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering there's also a somewhat different arrangement of &quot;ghostly elements&quot; in the Underworld book itself, i would say it's a case of wait and see about how the whole issue will be settled or messed with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T10:05:21-07:00","id":676525,"title":"","content":"What do you mean Baaldam? The corpse-element corresponding to Earth changed from Underworld Jade (in 1E) to Void (in 2E) but I don't know of any other changes to those elements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T12:57:52-07:00","id":676736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=673860#post673860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a kinda sorta interesting concept, my only real stumbling point with dragons of a different color being a thing is that the Dragon Blooded <i>predate</i> the creation of the underworld. Look at the kinds of hoops people have to jump through to corrupt the solar shards into abyssal shards. It just happening &quot;naturally&quot; to dragon bloods sometimes feels like something that's coming from the &quot;dragon blooded aren't REAL exalts like solars, lunars and sidereals&quot; PoV that seemed a fairly common one around the end of 2E's run.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was around for the tail end of that nonsense, it was pretty thoroughly shouted down by the time of Masters of Jade.<br /> <br /> Besides, it's not like the supposedly &quot;Real&quot; exalted are exactly as they were during their Initial Creation. Solars have their corrupted counterparts in the Abyssals and Infernals. Lunars have their Tattoos, Sidereals have Arcane Fate.<br /> <br /> A group of Dragonblooded who have been altered by centuries of exposure to the Underworld just seems like it'd be another interesting case of the Exalted being altered by the happenings all over Creation, or in this case out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 09-24-2015, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T13:05:13-07:00","id":676740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=673973#post673973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This begs the question of why a connection to the Underworld is relevant or necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the Underworld so utterly disconnected from Creation was one of the main things people complained about it in the previous edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T17:24:57-07:00","id":677063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=676525#post676525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean Baaldam? The corpse-element corresponding to Earth changed from Underworld Jade (in 1E) to Void (in 2E) but I don't know of any other changes to those elements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the issue is convoluted - going with &quot;dragons of a different color&quot;, corpse-elements would be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Prayer; Underworld Jade; Ghost-Flame; Blood; Bone. </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure either CoCD: Underworld or MoEP: Abyssals gives us a different list, but had no luck finding it at the moment,<br /> but your own comment about changes does seem to confirm my point such a list exists.<br /> <br /> <br /> And to finish the cake, the Scroll of Fallen Races while not talking of corpse-elements per se, gives us the following associations to the Dark Paths:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ash; Blood; Bones; Pyre-Flame; Void. </div> </div> </div>So, far from cut, dry &amp; settled the whole issue seems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T19:13:06-07:00","id":677135,"title":"","content":"Ah oops, I forgot Prayer was changed to Ash, because in my headcannon those are two names for the same element.<br /> <br /> Anyway, those two lists are indeed the 1E -&gt; 2E change.<br /> <br /> I think the writers wanted the Underworld to have reflections of the Elemental Poles that made more sense, and since Prayer isn't a physical substance and the Mouth of the Void is sort of where Mount Meru would be, they switched to Ash and Void. Although I think having prayer <i><b>be</b></i> a tangible substance in the Underworld would be really cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-24-2015, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T02:43:36-07:00","id":677436,"title":"","content":"In my headcanon it's Prayer, Jade, Ash, Bone and Blood.<br /> <br /> Ash is the cold memory of the energy and passion that fire represents; it seems more immediately resonant than a spooky coloured flame that eats through things like acid.<br /> Jade (representing Grave Goods) is much preferable to Void which to me is an unnecessary reminder that the Underworld is enemy territory. I also like the possibility of Underworld Elementals and don't think it'd be productive to have Oblivion manifest like that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 09-25-2015, 05:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T03:49:12-07:00","id":677450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=676740#post676740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the Underworld so utterly disconnected from Creation was one of the main things people complained about it in the previous edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>So just arbitrarily shove it in wherever? Yes, that will certainly make it feel like an organic and desirable part of the setting. It's almost as good as the Thousand Streams River.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T20:58:30-07:00","id":678467,"title":"","content":"See the thing that mostly inspires me to the whole Necrotic Dragonblooded is another posters Fanon that they shared with me a few years back in the old forum, probably during the Compass:Autocthonia, maybe earlier.<br /> <br /> The idea was something like Terrestrial Exalted based on the elements of the different worlds, Chiefly Underworld and Autocthonia and, interestingly enough Elloge (using elements of writing and language. I'm not entirely sure if said Terrsetrials worked exactly like Dragonblooded (especially the Ellogean ones), but were at about that level of power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 09-26-2015, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T00:26:44-07:00","id":678609,"title":"","content":"The only elements I'm interested in seeing DBs converted to are Kindness, Generosity, Laughter, Honesty, Loyalty, and Magic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T01:12:28-07:00","id":678627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea was something like Terrestrial Exalted based on the elements of the different worlds, Chiefly Underworld and Autocthonia and, interestingly enough Elloge (using elements of writing and language_. I'm not entirely sure if said Terrsetrials worked exactly like Dragonblooded (especially the Ellogean ones), but were at about that level of power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see how people would be drawn to that. I'm actually surprised how it doesn't seem to have been the focus for some kind of massively popular fan work in the manner of Nocturnals or Argent Witches, but can still see why people would have tried adapting the Dragon Blooded to them. Given the spirit of the new Edition, I'll be looking forward to people creating their own new Exalted to fit those concepts. I wouldn't personally call them Terrestrial just for semantic reasons of not being of the Earth, but for me to push that would be pedantic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> I think I may have misrepresented something earlier, so I want to clarify: I'm not against the idea of Dragon Blooded with an affinity for necromancy. I like that, and even like the idea of that affinity coming up from a strain in the bloodline inherited from some association with the Underworld. I think that the idea of something extra being added in there should be <i>subdued</i>, because I dislike the idea of Dragon Blooded as being about having sex with others in order to give their children extra powers*, but a few minor things such as a &quot;recessive&quot; magical affinity or some quirks out of being descended from a storm demon works for me.<br /> <br /> I was just disputing the idea that an association with the Underworld was something that the Terrestrial Exalted need to the extent that an absence of it is a lacking for them.<br /> <br /> * Nobody has said that, it's just an implication I've realised from my own statements, and want to nip in the bud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T01:15:19-07:00","id":678628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/669810-how-can-a-solar-glow-pink?p=678609#post678609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only elements I'm interested in seeing DBs converted to are Kindness, Generosity, Laughter, Honesty, Loyalty, and Magic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Problem is, they only have five castes.<br /> <br /> Maybe try it with alchemicals? =P<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}